{
 "meta": {
  "what": "Project Brownout: decided values for the 17 starting guns. Notion hub is the source of truth for rules; this file carries the per-gun numbers.",
  "updated": "2026-10-11",
  "notes": [
   "Names are placeholders. based_on = the Blackout gun the measurements come from.",
   "damage = body damage before armor. Armor reduces body damage 30/40/50% by tier; only tier 3 reduces head damage (30%).",
   "fire_interval_ms for semi-auto guns is a lower bound (how fast the footage player fired).",
   "ammo_in_s is when the mag counts as loaded; reload_s is the full animation. Estimated values are 55% of reload_s.",
   "Bullets are projectiles with travel time and gravity drop (no hitscan). bullet_speed_mps_start values are our own starting guesses; no measured Blackout numbers exist.",
   "Swap time = holster_s of the gun put away + draw_s of the gun brought up.",
   "recoil_measured is the on-screen pattern from the Blackout footage (degrees assume an 80 degree horizontal hip FOV); see weapons_brownout.json meta for caveats.",
   "Calibers match each gun's Blackout counterpart, except Savant (.45) and Splitter (9mm), which Logan swapped.",
   "2026-10-03 (phase 0): damage brought in line with the Weapons & Gunplay page (Blackout launch values for Icarus/Knocker/Rampage/Maddog; other non-snipers cut 10%; snipers unchanged); Twofer fires its two shots 100 ms apart; Long Barrel speed multiplier 1.1 to start, like every attachment effect (Blackout's was about 1.35, the value to tune toward).",
   "2026-10-04 (phase 3c): attachment effects moved into the attachments section (Attachments page: 10% each, Suppressor 35%); the Long Barrel's 1.1 bullet speed lives there now instead of ballistics. Effects are multipliers on the gun's own values. eye_distance_m is how far behind a sight's _ADS_Eye point the eye sits when aimed (Logan's 3c answer), tuned on the Gun Bench.",
   "2026-10-10 (phase 11a): magnified optics zoom only inside the lens (Logan), so the 2x, 4x and the built-in scopes (built_in_scope.eye_distance_m) sit 0.03 m behind their _ADS_Eye to start, leaving the scope body and the world around it in view; tune by feel.",
   "2026-10-11 (phase 11e): recoil_measured.ads_pattern_deg_first12 is read as where the view sat at each shot (an offset from the aim point), not as a kick per shot: the view springs toward the next shot's offset and settles back on release, so a spray sits around ads_up_mean_deg and peaks near ads_up_max_deg. New recoil_feel section: the kickback feel per gun class (render only, doesn't move where you aim); tune by feel."
  ]
 },
 "recoil_feel": {
  "notes": "Per shot the gun and arms slam back toward the camera (kickback_m) with a small pitch of the gun (gun_pitch_deg) and recover (recovery, higher = faster), and the view gets a small punch (punch_pitch_deg up, punch_roll_deg either way) that springs back without moving where you aim. Aimed in, the kickback is halved and the punch uses FeelSettings.FireKickAimed. Starting values from phase 10/11c's fixed kick, raised for kickback; tune by feel.",
